<div class=3D"section" id=3D"s1">
  <div class=3D"section-header">
    <div class=3D"section-num">01</div>
    <div class=3D"section-header-text">
      <h2>Install Python 3.11 or 3.12</h2>
      <p>The runtime that everything else depends on.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>Use <strong>Python 3.11 or 3.12</strong>. Do not use 3.9 or 3.10 =E2=
=80=94 some libraries we use require 3.11+. Do not use 3.13+ yet as some de=
pendencies are still catching up.</p>

  <div class=3D"os-tabs" id=3D"py-tabs">
    <div class=3D"os-tab active">macOS</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Windows</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Linux</div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"py-mac" class=3D"os-panel active">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">macOS =E2=80=94 using Homebrew</span>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Install Homebrew if you don't already have =
it</span>
/bin/bash -c <span class=3D"str">"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubuserconten=
t.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"</span>

<span class=3D"cm"># Install Python 3.12</span>
brew install python@3.12

<span class=3D"cm"># Verify</span>
python3 --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Python 3.12.x</span></pre>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"callout amber">
      <div class=3D"callout-title">macOS Note</div>
      macOS ships with an older Python. Always use <code>python3</code> in =
your terminal, not <code>python</code>.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"py-win" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">powershell</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">Windows</span>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Option 1 =E2=80=94 Installer (recommended)<=
/span>
<span class=3D"cm"># Visit: https://www.python.org/downloads/</span>
<span class=3D"cm"># Download Python 3.12.x =E2=86=92 Run the installer</sp=
an>
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=9C=85 Check "Add Python to PATH" during install =
=E2=80=94 important!</span>

<span class=3D"cm"># Option 2 =E2=80=94 winget</span>
winget install Python.Python.3.12

<span class=3D"cm"># Open a NEW terminal, then verify</span>
python --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Python 3.12.x</span></pre>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"callout amber">
      <div class=3D"callout-title">Windows Note</div>
      Always open a <strong>new terminal</strong> after installing Python s=
o PATH changes take effect.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"py-linux" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">Ubuntu / Debian</span>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre>sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev python3-pip -y

python3.12 --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Python 3.12.x</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

