<div class=3D"section" id=3D"s3">
  <div class=3D"section-header amber">
    <div class=3D"section-num">03</div>
    <div class=3D"section-header-text">
      <h2>Why Poetry? And How to Install It</h2>
      <p>We use Poetry instead of pip. Here is exactly why =E2=80=94 and ho=
w to get it running.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Why Not Just Use pip?</h3>
  <p>pip works fine for simple scripts. For any real project =E2=80=94 espe=
cially AI projects with complex, interacting dependencies =E2=80=94 pip cre=
ates problems that Poetry solves cleanly.</p>

  <div class=3D"table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>With pip</th><th>With Poetry</th></tr>=
</thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Reproducible installs</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 <code>requirements.txt</code> has n=
o lock. Versions drift between machines and over time.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 <code>poetry.lock</code> pins every=
 dependency to the exact version =E2=80=94 forever reproducible.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Virtual environments</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 You create, activate, and manage ve=
nvs manually every time.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 Poetry creates and manages a projec=
t venv automatically.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Dependency conflicts</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 Conflicts are discovered at runtime=
, often with cryptic errors.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 Poetry's resolver catches conflicts=
 at add-time before anything breaks.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Dev vs prod deps</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 Requires managing multiple <code>re=
quirements-*.txt</code> files manually.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 Built-in groups: <code>[dev]</code>=
, <code>[test]</code> =E2=80=94 clean, explicit separation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Project metadata</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 Spread across <code>setup.py</code>=
, <code>setup.cfg</code>, <code>MANIFEST.in</code>.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 Everything in one <code>pyproject.t=
oml</code> =E2=80=94 the modern Python standard.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Team collaboration</strong></td>
          <td class=3D"cross">=E2=9C=97 "Works on my machine" is a real and=
 common problem.</td>
          <td class=3D"check">=E2=9C=93 Commit <code>poetry.lock</code> =E2=
=86=92 every teammate gets an identical environment.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>AI projects are especially dependency-fragile. LangChain, LangGraph, O=
penAI SDK, Pydantic, and their transitive dependencies interact in complex =
ways. A single version mismatch can silently break tool calling or agent ex=
ecution in ways that are very hard to debug. Poetry's lockfile eliminates t=
his entire class of problem.</p>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Install Poetry</h3>

  <div class=3D"callout red">
    <div class=3D"callout-title">Important</div>
    Do <strong>not</strong> install Poetry with <code>pip install poetry</c=
ode> inside a project. Install it globally using pipx or the official insta=
ller, so it stays isolated from the projects it manages.
  </div>

  <div class=3D"os-tabs" id=3D"poetry-tabs">
    <div class=3D"os-tab active">macOS</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Windows</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Linux</div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"poetry-mac" class=3D"os-panel active">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">macOS =E2=80=94 via pipx (recommended)</=
span>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Install pipx =E2=80=94 the right tool for i=
nstalling Python CLI apps globally</span>
brew install pipx
pipx ensurepath

<span class=3D"cm"># Install Poetry</span>
pipx install poetry

<span class=3D"cm"># Verify</span>
poetry --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Poetry (version 2.4.1)</span>

<span class=3D"cm"># Configure Poetry to create the venv inside the project=
 folder (makes IDE integration easier)</span>
poetry config virtualenvs.in-project <span class=3D"kw">true</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"poetry-win" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">powershell</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">Windows =E2=80=94 official installer (Po=
werShell)</span>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Run the official installer</span>
(Invoke-WebRequest -Uri https://install.python-poetry.org -UseBasicParsing)=
.Content | py -

<span class=3D"cm"># The installer prints the PATH to add. It looks like:</=
span>
<span class=3D"cm"># %APPDATA%\Python\Scripts</span>
<span class=3D"cm"># Add it: Start =E2=86=92 Search "Environment Variables"=
 =E2=86=92 System Variables =E2=86=92 PATH =E2=86=92 Edit =E2=86=92 Add it<=
/span>

<span class=3D"cm"># Open a NEW terminal, then verify</span>
poetry --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Poetry (version 2.4.1)</span>

poetry config virtualenvs.in-project true</pre>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"callout amber">
      <div class=3D"callout-title">Windows Note</div>
      If <code>py</code> is not found, replace it with <code>python</code>.=
 Always open a fresh terminal after installation.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"poetry-linux" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header">
        <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
        <span class=3D"code-label">Linux =E2=80=94 official installer</span=
>
        <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Official installer</span>
curl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python3 -

<span class=3D"cm"># Add to PATH =E2=80=94 paste into ~/.bashrc or ~/.zshrc=
</span>
<span class=3D"kw">export</span> PATH=3D<span class=3D"str">"$HOME/.local/b=
in:$PATH"</span>

<span class=3D"cm"># Reload your shell</span>
source ~/.bashrc

<span class=3D"cm"># Verify</span>
poetry --version
<span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 Poetry (version 2.4.1)</span>

poetry config virtualenvs.in-project <span class=3D"kw">true</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"callout green" style=3D"margin-top:16px">
    <div class=3D"callout-title">Key Poetry Commands to Remember</div>
    <code>poetry add &lt;package&gt;</code> =E2=80=94 add a dependency and =
update the lockfile<br>
    <code>poetry install</code> =E2=80=94 install all deps from lockfile (r=
eproducible)<br>
    <code>poetry run python script.py</code> =E2=80=94 run a script inside =
the managed venv<br>
    <code>poetry shell</code> =E2=80=94 activate the venv in your current t=
erminal session
  </div>
</div>

<div class=3D"divider"></div>

