<div class=3D"section" id=3D"s7">
  <div class=3D"section-header" style=3D"border-left-color:var(--text-muted=
)">
    <div class=3D"section-num">07</div>
    <div class=3D"section-header-text">
      <h2>Set Up Git &amp; GitHub</h2>
      <p>Version control for all your course work. Push to GitHub so your w=
ork is backed up.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Step 1 =E2=80=94 Install Git</h3>

  <div class=3D"os-tabs" id=3D"git-tabs">
    <div class=3D"os-tab active">macOS</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Windows</div>
    <div class=3D"os-tab">Linux</div>
  </div>

  <div id=3D"git-mac" class=3D"os-panel active">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header"><span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span><butt=
on class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
      <pre>brew install git
git --version   <span class=3D"cm"># =E2=86=92 git version 2.x.x</span></pr=
e>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id=3D"git-win" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header"><span class=3D"code-lang">powershell</span=
><button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
      <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Download and install from: https://git-scm.=
com/download/win</span>
<span class=3D"cm"># OR via winget:</span>
winget install Git.Git
<span class=3D"cm"># Open a new terminal, then verify:</span>
git --version</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id=3D"git-linux" class=3D"os-panel">
    <div class=3D"code-block">
      <div class=3D"code-header"><span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span><butt=
on class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
      <pre>sudo apt install git -y
git --version</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Step 2 =E2=80=94 Configure Git Identity</h3>
  <div class=3D"code-block">
    <div class=3D"code-header">
      <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
      <span class=3D"code-label">One-time global config</span>
      <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre>git config --global user.name <span class=3D"str">"Your Name"</spa=
n>
git config --global user.email <span class=3D"str">"you@example.com"</span>
git config --global init.defaultBranch main</pre>
  </div>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Step 3 =E2=80=94 Initialise the Repo &amp; Create .giti=
gnore</h3>
  <div class=3D"code-block">
    <div class=3D"code-header">
      <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
      <span class=3D"code-label">Inside agentic-ai-course/</span>
      <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Initialise git</span>
git init

<span class=3D"cm"># Create .gitignore</span>
cat &gt; .gitignore &lt;&lt;EOF
.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/
EOF

<span class=3D"cm"># First commit</span>
git add .
git commit -m <span class=3D"str">"Initial project setup"</span></pre>
  </div>

  <h3 class=3D"sub">Step 4 =E2=80=94 Push to GitHub</h3>
  <ol class=3D"steps-list">
    <li>Go to <strong>github.com</strong> =E2=86=92 sign in =E2=86=92 click=
 <strong>New repository</strong></li>
    <li>Name it <code>agentic-ai-course</code>, set it to <strong>Private</=
strong>, do NOT initialise with a README</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Create repository</strong></li>
    <li>Copy the two commands GitHub shows you (they look like the block be=
low)</li>
  </ol>

  <div class=3D"code-block">
    <div class=3D"code-header">
      <span class=3D"code-lang">bash</span>
      <span class=3D"code-label">Connect and push to GitHub</span>
      <button class=3D"copy-btn">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <pre><span class=3D"cm"># Replace YOUR_USERNAME with your actual GitHub=
 username</span>
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/agentic-ai-course.gi=
t
git push -u origin main</pre>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"callout blue">
    <div class=3D"callout-title">GitHub Authentication</div>
    If GitHub asks for a password, use a <strong>Personal Access Token</str=
ong> (not your account password). Generate one at: GitHub =E2=86=92 Setting=
s =E2=86=92 Developer Settings =E2=86=92 Personal Access Tokens =E2=86=92 T=
okens (classic) =E2=86=92 Generate new token. Select the <code>repo</code> =
scope.
  </div>
</div>

<div class=3D"divider"></div>

